<section
  class="how-it-works"
  id="how-it-works"
  aria-labelledby="how-it-works-title"
>
  <div class="section-inner">
    <h2 id="how-it-works-title">Four stages, one commit, your decision</h2>
    <ol class="pipeline">
      <li class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-marker">
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.6"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path d="M12 3v18M5 8l7-5 7 5" />
            <path d="M5 14v5h14v-5" />
          </svg>
          <span class="step-number">01</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Opt in.</h3>
        <p>
          Label a GitHub issue <code>factory-kit</code>. It needs acceptance
          criteria, and nothing written in the issue can widen what the agents
          may do.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-marker">
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.6"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path d="M8 6H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v11a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h11a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-3" />
            <path d="m9 15 1-4 9-9 4 4-9 9-5 1Z" />
          </svg>
          <span class="step-number">02</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Implement and review.</h3>
        <p>
          A Hermes worker implements the issue in an isolated git worktree. A
          separate reviewer session checks the diff against the criteria. One
          fix round is allowed.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-marker">
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.6"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path d="M3 12h18M12 3v18" />
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" />
            <path d="m8 12 2.5 2.5L16 9" />
          </svg>
          <span class="step-number">03</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Verify and preview.</h3>
        <p>
          factory-kit opens a PR for the reviewed commit, waits for your
          required checks on that exact head, publishes a preview of it and
          smoke-tests the URL.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="pipeline-step">
        <div class="step-marker">
          <svg
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.6"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path d="m5 12 4 4L19 6" />
            <path d="M12 22a10 10 0 1 0-10-10" />
          </svg>
          <span class="step-number">04</span>
        </div>
        <h3>Approve and merge.</h3>
        <p>
          You approve that commit. factory-kit rechecks head, base, checks and
          preview, squash-merges with an expected-head guard, and reports the
          merge SHA that GitHub recorded.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <a class="build-cta" href="https://github.com/luongnv89">
      Follow the build on GitHub
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

